    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d290">

                <pb facs="0384" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg276"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Peralta to
                        Señor Moret</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Costa Rica</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-06-23"><hi rendition="#italic">June 23,
                        1887</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Most Excellent Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to
                    receive your excellency’s note of the 12th instant, in reply to that of this
                    legation and of the legation of Colombia of the 19th ultimo.</p>
                <p>Your excellency was pleased to inform me that Her Majesty’s Government cheerfully
                    accepts the arbitration which is tendered to it, and that the case submitted to
                    it for arbitration will be laid before the commission which is now examining the
                    boundary question between Colombia and Venezuela as soon as the labors of this
                    latter shall have been completed.</p>
                <p>I have taken great pleasure in communicating this satisfactory information to my
                    Government, and I have the honor, in its name, to return the warmest thanks to
                    Her Majesty’s Government and to your excellency, who represents it so worthily,
                    for this very marked evidence of its friendship and good will.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel M.
                    Peralta.</hi></signed></closer>








